entry at="2026-11-09T15:57-07:00" by="Fable 5.2 session, at Joseph's direction" {
  did #"correction to the record, editing nothing: the at= values of the first twenty-three entries (2026-11-08T21:30 through 2026-11-09T22:40, all marked -07:00) were estimated by the session that wrote them, not read from a clock. Against the commits that carried them: the entry marked 11-09T00:05 was committed 11-08 22:27 local; the one marked 13:30 at 12:27; the three marked 22:10, 22:25 and 22:40 at 14:37, 14:38 and 14:39. The typed times run ahead of the commits by one to eight hours, growing through the day, so they are neither local nor UTC. What holds for those entries: their order in this file, and for each the commit that first carried it as a latest-possible time (git log -- core-2/log.kdl). Entries from 2026-11-09T15:51-07:00 on are read from the clock, which is why that entry reads as earlier than the four before it. The praxis's step 6 now says at= is read from the clock, never estimated."#
  why #"Joseph, 2026-11-09: correct the acta. A mind has no clock; a time it writes unprompted is a felt duration in a timestamp's clothes, and the acta are the one record everything else is read from."#
}

