entry at="2026-11-09T16:21-07:00" by="Fable 5.2 session, at Joseph's objection" {
  did #"verisectorium's invariants cut to the three that are true of the whole and of none of its parts: its ontology declares at least one determinant (until now only a relation note), and Joseph's two (one canonical projection, true as stated; provisional claims only the suggestion). Removed as other terms' business: assertion within warrant at a steady state (steady·state's), every piece of a declared kind (now stated in veritoid and in segment, each of exactly one kind), nothing changed by hand (changeset's). Segment no longer restates the canonical-projection invariant. The rule is written into def/README and the def template: an invariant is stated once, in the def of the thing that is broken when it fails."#
  why #"Joseph, 2026-11-09: the def "still states invariants that it has no business stating. I don't want to have to hunt all over the definitions and segments to figure out where the 'content has a kind' invariant is." A def that restates its parts' invariants is the restates failure the segment def's own notes warn of: repaired by ceasing to restate, not by keeping copies in step."#
}

