entry at="2026-11-09T16:29-07:00" by="Fable 5.2 session, after Joseph's challenge and a fork's whole read" {
  did #"correction: the earlier actum's "what I found" about the first core rested on nine of its def files read for invariants and working notes only, on the assumption that the rest of each was text shared with group-mates. A fork read the nine whole. The assumption held for seven (steady·state, steady·time, work·time, working·state, theory·claim, veritoid, veritoid·kind) and was false for two written alone (truth·determinant, verisectorium). What that read found uncarried is now in working notes, each quote checked against the file: dimension (completeness as a determinant and as the first answer to softening-to-tautologies; several dimensions bearing on one determinant; "in the service of"; standards versus ways of finding out; determinant change and recorded acts; shared vocabulary; "fitness" reversed), kind (the admission rule for kinds), frontier (a rule due and unrun), act (a lapsed check is still a record of the checker), verisectorium (two sentences). Steady·state's Definition said a working state "is never the theory"; it says never the verisectorium."#
