entry at="2026-11-09T16:38-07:00" by="Fable 5.2 session, at Joseph's question whether the lesson had landed" {
  did #"read the first core's truth-determinant and verisectorium defs whole, which until now I had only through a fork's report and greps for its quotes. Two working notes on dimension that I had attached from that report are rewritten: "several dimensions can bear on one determinant" is, in its source, one dimension with two rungs here and no argument against determinant being a mark (I had called it the strongest reason to doubt that); completeness, read with its table and remark, points at a possible simplification, that an ordinary completeness dimension on a projection could replace the "more strongly" clause in the sense of better. The praxis gains step 0: read a thing whole, yourself, before integrating, superseding, discarding or attaching it, and say what was read by whom."#
  why #"Joseph, 2026-11-09: "at least read the thing before throwing it away or blindly attaching it to a segment". I had done both with these two files."#
}

